com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-28T09:33:49Z","updated_at":"2024-04-28T09:33:49Z","body":"It's there just as a simple check that we're running in an environment that looks at least a little bit like the ones on which we test. Folks do try and run these things on weird unsupported Linux-like OSs sometimes and if the format of this data is too different from what we expect then other things will go wrong.\r\n\r\nHowever in this case you're right, the regular Linux kernel can, in some configurations, yield an extra `wait_sum` line here:\r\n\r\nhttps://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/kernel/sched/core.c?id=57865f397001f592817eea513251705d45d000af#n11113\r\n\r\nI think we shouldn't simply remove this assertion. Instead I'd rather we strengthened it to say that the file format is roughly what we expect here, but to tolerate extra values added in future kernel versions since this seems not to be considered a breaking change to the kernel.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/2081410391/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284